{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And they remembered</b> (ויזכרו), <b>their Rock</b> (צורם) — like חזקם (their strength)." "<b>And El Elyon was their redeemer</b> — and the name that redeemed them is El Elyon, who can do upon the earth and its inhabitants all that He desires. Now ויזכירו is with the mouth, like: \"and the burden of HaShem you shall no longer mention\" (ומשא ה׳ לא תזכרו עוד), and the proof: \"and their heart was not steadfast\" (ולבם לא נכון)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:10.698105667Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}